the breeding ground of crime and delinquency in all other social ills. And here's Robert Moses, addressing the audience after Kaysen. I believe that when the dust of the housing, battles has settled, this cooperative non-profit village will go down in history. It is one of the very best. The housing battles Moses is referring to is likely the community opposition to the Penn South development and others like it. During each project, old neighborhoods had been destroyed and resonance displaced.
这里是犯罪、青少年 delinquency（违法乱纪）以及所有其他社会弊病的温床。接着是罗伯特·摩西，他在凯森之后向观众发表讲话。我相信，当住房之战的硝烟散去，这个合作非营利村庄将载入史册。它是最好的之一。摩西所指的住房之战，很可能是社区对宾夕法尼亚南区开发项目及其他类似项目的反对。在每个项目期间，旧社区都被摧毁，居民流离失所。

