Robert Caro, author of the power broker, estimated that Moses evicted 250,000 people to build highways in New York City. and another 250,000 for urban renewal projects like slum clearance and housing development. Efforts to rehouse the displaced were half-hearted at best. Robert Moses was infamously dismissive of his detractors, saying once that the critics build nothing, and also this classic. You're never going to get unanimous approval. There must be people who are discommoted inconvenienced or call it what you will on the old theory,
《权力掮客》的作者罗伯特·卡罗估计，摩西为了在纽约市修建高速公路驱逐了25万人，为了城市更新项目（如清除贫民窟和住房开发）又驱逐了25万人。重新安置流离失所者的努力充其量只能算是敷衍了事。罗伯特·摩西对批评者的态度出了名的不屑一顾，他曾说过批评者什么也没建造，还有这个经典名言：你永远不可能获得一致同意。总会有人感到不便、困扰或随你怎么说，根据旧理论，

