You know, union-sponsored nonprofit housing was affordable to a plumbent. or a garment worker with a steady job and a union contract. It was not necessarily affordable to a lower level of the working class. The poorer segment of slum dwellers were more likely to be African American or Puerto Rican. So, in fact, a lot of the union co-ops were almost all white. You know, I mean, in some cases, they were literally all white. They saw the world in kind of class terms.
你知道，工会资助的非营利住房对于水管工或拥有稳定工作和工会合同的服装工人来说是负担得起的。但对于更低阶层的工人阶级来说，它不一定负担得起。贫民窟中较穷的阶层更有可能是非裔美国人或波多黎各人。因此，事实上，许多工会合作公寓几乎全是白人。你知道，我的意思是，在某些情况下，它们字面意义上就是全白人。他们以某种阶级视角来看待世界。

