00:17:30.000 --> 00:18:10.000
Because they saw that this gave people a stake in the community, that they would not have if they were mere renters in their minds. Apart from displaced community members, Robert Moses and the UHF had another prominent critic around this time, the writer and activist Jane Jacobs. And what she was saying is like, no, no, no, you know, these places that you're so quick to condemn, both physically condemn and like morally condemn, are actually functioning communities. And that when you build new housing, what you're doing is destroying community and you're building something sterile from which no community can emerge.
因为他们看到这赋予了人们对社区的归属感，而如果他们只是租客的话，在他们看来就不会有这种归属感。除了流离失所的社区成员，罗伯特·摩西和UHF在这一时期还有另一个著名的批评者——作家兼活动家简·雅各布斯。而她的观点是，不，不，不，你知道，这些你们急于谴责的地方——无论是从物理上还是从道德上谴责——实际上是功能健全的社区。当你建造新住房时，你所做的是在摧毁社区，并建造一个无法产生任何社区意识的贫瘠之物。

