The tide was shifting against modernist architecture, against Robert Moses and his urban renewal policies. And soon, against the project of big government liberalism that made all of the this building possible. But for now, the United Housing Foundation and Robert Moses still had momentum and money. And their biggest project was still ahead of them. Not just their biggest project, actually, but one of the biggest residential housing developments ever constructed, 35 skyscrapers that would house more than 15,000 families. Coming up, a project that will ultimately destroy the United Housing Foundation and the cooperative housing movement that Abraham Kaysen had built.
潮流正在转向反对现代主义建筑，反对罗伯特·摩西及其城市更新政策。不久之后，也开始反对让所有这些建设成为可能的大政府自由主义项目。但就目前而言，联合住房基金会和罗伯特·摩西仍然拥有势头和资金。他们最大的项目还在前方。事实上，不仅是他们最大的项目，而且是有史以来建造的最大住宅开发项目之一，35座摩天大楼将容纳超过1.5万户家庭。接下来，一个最终将摧毁联合住房基金会以及亚伯拉罕·凯森所建立的合作住房运动的项目即将登场。

