And the story goes that people leave the buildings, they come, they're helping, stranded. travelers. They're bringing them in. They're giving them like hot tea or hot cocoa. Meanwhile, kids are having like snowball fights. And so it becomes celebrated in this kind of Co-Upt City mythology as like the creation of a community. It was kind of proving the critics wrong. Yeah, exactly. The architecture did not stand in the way of creating a community at all. Anne-Marie wasn't there for the Blizzard, but she actually did grow up in Co-op City. And she remembers a pretty idyllic childhood there, riding her bike around the vast green spaces that surrounded the buildings, playing with the other kids, and then as a teenager, just wandering around
有传言说，人们离开大楼，过来提供帮助，帮助那些滞留的旅客。把他们接进来。给他们热茶或热可可。与此同时，孩子们在打雪仗。因此，它在合作城的这种神话中被颂扬为社区的创建。这有点证明了批评者的错误。是的，完全如此。这种建筑风格根本没有阻碍社区的建立。安娜-玛丽当时不在暴风雪现场，但她确实在合作城长大。她对那里有着相当田园诗般的童年记忆，骑着自行车穿梭于环绕建筑群的广阔绿地，与其他孩子一起玩耍，到了青少年时期，就在周围闲逛，

