looking for any kind of fun. I remember being like 13 years old when there's this big mall that opened and it had the first store that opened, in my memory at least, was a hardware store. And me and all these other kids my age just went to the hardware store just to like look at wrenches or whatever because there was like nothing to do. Great place to be a kid, boring place to be a teenager. In other words, this place was basically the suburbs. Co-op City and a lot of other UHF cooperatives were providing alternatives to suburbia that helped convince the middle class to stay in the city.
寻找任何能带来乐趣的东西。我记得我13岁的时候，有一个大型购物中心开业了，在我记忆中，里面开的第一家店至少是一家五金店。我和其他同龄的孩子去五金店只是为了看扳手什么的，因为实在没事可做。作为小孩子来说是个好地方，作为青少年来说则是个无聊的地方。换句话说，这个地方基本上就是郊区。合作城和许多其他UHF合作公寓为郊区生活提供了替代方案，有助于说服中产阶级留在城市里。

